. 
.         
.         * Changes from PAP:
.         * - in the PAP I preregistered a panel logit regression with fixed ef
> fects.
.         * First, a mistake: one cannot run xtlogit with fixed effects, so 
.         * I would have had to drop the FEs. Second, since the xtlogit did not
>  converge
.         * on the 5% sample, I decided to run a linear OLS regression with fix
> ed 
.         * effects instead and keep the clustering of the standard errors at 
.         * individual level. I decided for this before seeing results in the f
> ull 
.         * sample because xtlogit relies on switchers in the dep var for ident
> ification 
.         * and I do not expect many of them even in the full sample. The OLS 
.         * regression should give an OK approximation. 
.         * - I calculated age differently, using syear instead of pgpiyear, si
> nce 
.         * pgpiyear was only recorded in some years.
.         * - I calculated age differently, using syear instead of pgpiyear, si
> nce 
.         * pgpiyear was only recorded in some years.
.         * - For years of education, I used pgbilzeit instead of pgbilzt, as t
> he 
.         * second variable wasn't in SOEP Core, but in SOEP IS (misunderstandi
> ng).
.         * - For living in East/West Germany, I used sampreg instead of bgsamp
> reg, 
.         * as this was the correct variable in SOEP Core (misunderstanding).
.         * - I restricted the estimation sample to those in private households
> , with
.         * pop 1 or 2.
.         * - I dropped the migration background as a control, because it canno
> t be used
.         * in a regression with individual FEs (since it is constant within pe
> rson). It 
.         * was a mistake to include it in a FE model in the PAP.
.         * - Unspecified in PAP: the baseline NUTS region is Berlin.
.         
.         
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS *
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[total_daughters]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[total_daughters]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[total_daughters] / _se[total_daughters]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation of directionality
.                 scalar coef_total_daughters = _b[total_daughters]

.                 local interpretation "negative coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

. 
